Sval: the crash dialog sends no Glean crash ping

Mozilla's crash reporter client starts Glean when the dialog opens and
queues a crash ping, with a client id, for incoming.telemetry.mozilla.org.
It decides whether that ping may upload by reading
datareporting.healthreport.uploadEnabled from the profile's prefs.js, and
treats an absent pref as true. Sval locks the pref false in its default
prefs, which never reach prefs.js, so that check cannot see Sval's choice.
The dialog starts no Glean and sends no ping. The report itself leaves only
when the user ticks the send box.

Starting Glean also takes the exclusive lock on Crash Reports/glean/
crashping.pid. In Sval's release build the dialog holds that lock until
the user closes it, and every later crash's dialog and every --ping-cleanup
run waits on it with no window.

Gecko's CrashManager runs the client with --ping-cleanup on each
maintenance pass, whatever the upload pref says. Glean started that way on
a store that once had upload on queues a deletion-request ping for the same
server, so the CrashManager starts the client for no ping at all.

Mozilla's glean_ping test becomes sval_no_glean_ping, which checks that no
ping is sent, and test_sval_no_crash_ping.js checks the maintenance pass.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/crashes/CrashManager.in.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/crashes/CrashManager.in.sys.mjs
index fb88aea56a..e87de01c80 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/crashes/CrashManager.in.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/crashes/CrashManager.in.sys.mjs
@@ -175,7 +175,10 @@ export var CrashManager = function (options) {
 
   // Tests may disable the Glean ping to avoid unnecessary overhead of invoking
   // the crash reporter client.
-  this._disableGleanPing = false;
+  // Sval: no crash ping is sent and no ping cleanup runs. Glean started by
+  // --ping-cleanup with upload off on a store that had a client id queues a
+  // deletion-request ping for Mozilla's telemetry.
+  this._disableGleanPing = true;
 
   // The CrashStore currently attached to this object.
   this._store = null;
